4. Functional Requirements
4.1 Local Directory Indexer & Feature Extraction (FR-1)
Recursive Folder Scanning: Scan user-selected local image directories for common raster formats (PNG, JPEG, WebP) and track file additions, modifications, and deletions.
Multimodal Embedding Generation: Compute dense vision embeddings for every indexed image using OpenAI CLIP or SigLIP.
OCR Text Extraction: Extract visible text strings from lecture screenshots, slides, and memes using EasyOCR or Tesseract OCR and store extracted text alongside image metadata.
Color Palette Heuristics: Compute dominant color palettes and color-space distributions for each image to enable color-based filtering and hybrid ranking.
4.2 Local Vector Index & Cross-Modal Retrieval (FR-2)
Sub-Millisecond Vector Retrieval: Index all normalized vision embeddings inside a local FAISS index to achieve sub-millisecond nearest-neighbor search latency.
Cross-Modal Query Modes:
Text-to-Image: Encode natural language "vibe" or concept queries via the text encoder of CLIP / SigLIP and retrieve top-k matching images from FAISS.
Image-to-Image: Query the FAISS index using an existing image's embedding vector to surface visually similar images.
Sketch-to-Image: Encode user drawings from the live sketch-pad into the shared embedding space and combine with structural/color heuristics for retrieval.
Hybrid Search Fusion: Combine semantic vector similarity scores (FAISS), OCR text matching (EasyOCR / Tesseract OCR), and dominant color-space heuristics into a unified ranking pipeline.
4.3 Dimensionality Reduction & Theme Clustering (FR-3)
2D/3D Coordinate Projection: Project high-dimensional CLIP / SigLIP embeddings into 2D and 3D spatial coordinates using UMAP and t-SNE.
Visual Theme / Vibe Clustering: Group projected coordinates into thematic clusters so visually and conceptually related assets (e.g., lecture notes, code snippets, memes, landscapes) form distinct neighborhoods.
4.4 Interactive Frontend & 3D Galaxy Explorer (FR-4)
2D/3D Embedding Galaxy Explorer: Render an interactive spatial canvas where users can pan, zoom, rotate, and inspect clusters of thousands of images in 2D or 3D space.
Live Sketch-Pad Query Tool: Provide an interactive drawing canvas allowing users to sketch rough shapes and colors and trigger live sketch-to-image retrieval.
Semantic & Heuristic Search Filters: Support combined filtering by natural language prompt, OCR keyword match, dominant color swatches, and cluster tags.
4.5 Batch Performance Optimization & Duplicate Detection (FR-5)
Quantized Inference Pipeline: Export vision-language models to ONNX Runtime with FP16 quantization to maximize batch indexing throughput on local hardware.
Duplicate & Near-Duplicate Detection: Identify exact and near-duplicate images using cosine similarity thresholds in the FAISS embedding space and surface them for cleanup or grouping.
