6. Performance Targets, Success Criteria & Learning Outcomes
System Verification Criteria
Retrieval Latency: Sub-millisecond vector search query execution over the indexed dataset via FAISS.
Scale Validation: End-to-end indexing, duplicate detection, and interactive 2D/3D visualization verified on a chaotic multi-thousand-image local dataset.
Cross-Modal Accuracy: Verified retrieval across all four query modalities (natural language vibe, OCR text, live sketch-pad, and dominant color palette / image similarity).
Core Learning Outcomes
Contrastive Multimodal Pipelines: Mastering OpenAI CLIP and SigLIP embeddings and end-to-end cross-modal retrieval workflows.
Vector Indexing & Manifold Visualization: Implementing FAISS indexing alongside high-dimensional projection with UMAP and t-SNE.
Hybrid Search Architecture: Fusing OCR (EasyOCR / Tesseract OCR), color-space heuristics, and semantic vectors into a unified retrieval engine.
Local AI Application Delivery: Shipping a quantized (ONNX Runtime), local-first multimodal desktop search engine with an interactive 3D embedding explorer.
